helmd - security analysis engineering agent bundle
====================================================

WHAT THIS PACKAGE CONTAINS
--------------------------
helmd is a bundle for the DeepSeek Harness (dsh) agent runtime that turns the
agent into a security-analysis assistant. It ships:

- Domain analysis tools and playbooks for binary, mobile (Android), web,
  network-protocol and malware sample triage (static analysis, hashing,
  entropy, string/import tables, pcap review, evidence handling).
- Reference documents describing exploitation techniques, common vulnerable
  services and ports, web/protocol attack playbooks, and payload corpora used
  to support defensive analysis, reverse engineering, CTF work and
  authorized penetration testing.
- A toolbox that runs locally on the operator's machine and only acts on
  targets explicitly supplied by the operator during the session.

INTENDED LEGITIMATE USE
-----------------------
- Security research and defensive analysis (understanding samples, IoCs,
  attack chains) on systems the operator owns or is explicitly authorized
  to test.
- Reverse engineering, malware triage and incident-response support.
- Security education, including capture-the-flag exercises and coursework.

AUTHORIZATION AND RESPONSIBILITY
--------------------------------
The bundle does not target anything by itself: every scan, exploit check or
network interaction is operator-initiated against operator-supplied targets.
Operators are responsible for obtaining authorization, complying with
applicable law, and audit logging. The package ships no self-propagating
code, no persistence mechanism, no credential harvesting and no command-and-
control infrastructure.

